#{[17592186399656 #edb/ref 1080 "No intersection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399656 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399656 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d6d8eeca-91ef-5d44-a9a1-da7d1707ffce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402256 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33987" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402256 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402256 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,5,9⟩+t⟨4,-1,6⟩,\\,Π:-2x+4y+2z-16=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402256 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cbfd2820-3a30-53a2-832d-407032fe3cf1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402256 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+2z-16 & =0 \\\\ -2x+4y+2z & =16 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ ⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2(3+4t)+4(5-t)+2(9+6t) & =16 \\\\ -6-8t+20-4t+18+12t & =16 \\\\ 32 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402257 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402257 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402257 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402257 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402257 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402257 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402257 #edb/ref 1077 "sel